# interplay_session_workstation: One head, two apps. Version negotiation (0x100 answered with 0xf5, a request with bit 31 ignored), EFI's frame presented and encoded, device info, then the driver: task 0 with two backings, EFI off before the display page connects (the handover), a frame and the cursor. Tasks 1 and 2 run blit, compute (add_one) and render work on child FIFOs 1 and 2, task 2's exec waiting on task 1's stamp (a barrier); both render the same triangle, so their render results are the same bytes. Suspend and resume on a fresh device in the middle: the resumed device replays the cursor, runs the same work with the tasks swapped between the child FIFOs, and every result equals its pre-suspend twin. A frame after the resume, then orderly teardown and release.
